===Use the celestial globe to alter the firmament and reveal the past.{{subst:void|<!--104040701-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location="Fortress of Dome" Eye of Twilight|Seliose's past seems to diverge greatly from what was told in bygone stories. Now, accompanied by her two mythical companion beasts from ages past, we stand poised to unveil the ancient and hidden truths.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

:{{DIcon|undefined}} Operate celestial globe
:'''Hyacine:''' ..."The turn of dawn and dusk, commanding the celestial globe..."
:'''Hyacine:''' "Embrace the clouds, Celestial Mural."
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' Ha... look who we've caught &mdash; an old-fashioned disciple of the ancient god!
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' The frail Titan was conquered long ago by the mighty warrior goddess. Now they're nothing more than rusted scrap, left in the forge to decay over countless years.
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' Surrender to us, relic of a bygone era! We'll reshape your clouded mind and grant you a place alongside your kin in Seliose's glory...
:'''Helpless Old Disciple:''' Your so-called "reshaping" is nothing more than torment, both in body and mind.
:'''Helpless Old Disciple:''' No... I'd rather die than give in to hypocrites like you, hiding behind empty faith and wielding power as you please!
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' Hahaha! Take a good look at this pathetic fool! Do you see it? What a laughable hypocrite!
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' You're one of the Sunfolk, aren't you?
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' When you oppressed your own under the guise of faith, leaving countless souls to suffer endlessly under the scorching sun &mdash; did you ever consider that even the fiercest sun could one day fall?
:'''Helpless Old Disciple:''' I... I once thought...
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' Spare us your empty excuses, relic of the old world. "I'd rather die than give in to hypocrites like you, hiding behind empty faith and wielding power as you please!" &mdash;
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' &mdash; You've already sentenced yourself. All we're doing is following through.
:'''Ruthless New Believer:''' Do it. Make it clean. A single, sharp cut across the neck.
:'''Helpless Old Disciple:''' No, no... NO!!!
:'''Hyacine:''' ...
:'''Phainon:''' ...The creations shaped by Kephale in their image failed to inherit their compassion and acceptance.
:'''Phainon:''' Are you alright, Hyacine?
:'''Hyacine:''' I'm fine, Lord Phainon. I... expected this.
:'''Hyacine:''' It's just... thinking about the vision Seliose held before declaring war on the Titan... this sight is deeply heartbreaking.
:'''Hyacine:''' ...Let's move on.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Witness the true history of the Skyfolk.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Listen to Hyacine's summary.
:{{tx}}

:'''Lunabis:''' Seliose possessed the strength to slay gods...
:'''Lunabis:''' Yet, she failed to sever the cycle of karma rooted deeply in humanity's hearts.

:{{DIcon|undefined}} Operate celestial globe
:'''Hyacine:''' ..."The turn of dawn and dusk, commanding the celestial globe..."
:'''Hyacine:''' "Drive out the gods, Celestial Mural."
:'''Dan Heng:''' Could that be...
:'''Phainon:''' But... how is that possible?
:'''Dispirited Old Believer:''' Please... help us, the forsaken Skyfolk...
:'''Dispirited Old Believer:''' ...Lady Caenis, you are the strong one who follows the path of shadows.
:'''Phainon:''' The "Cleaners"...! Did the Skyfolk conspire with them?
:'''Dispirited Old Believer:''' Word has it you hunt those with golden blood, all in your quest to cleanse the world of the filth of those cursed offspring.
:'''Dispirited Old Believer:''' Deliver justice for us. The witch with golden blood struck down the proud Eye of Twilight, desecrating their divine grace. Yet, it is we, the devout denizens of the sky, who are forced to pay the price!
:'''"Caenis":''' I can smell your despair, Skyfolk... The Cleaners are on the side of mortals. Together, we'll erase that blasphemous bloodline from this world.
:'''"Caenis":''' The Daythunder Knight and her fantastic creatures are far too strong. No one can hope to defeat them in a direct fight. But we'll show you every trick, every strategy you can use to turn the tide...
:'''Phainon:''' In their desperation, those ancient disciples were willing to do anything &mdash; even ally themselves with the Cleaners.
:'''Phainon:''' But I'm guessing their plan failed, didn't it?
:'''Solabis:''' Those assassins were vicious, but not foolish. They never actually dared to attack Seliose.
:'''Solabis:''' They weren't driven by any genuine desire to help the oppressed. Their true targets were the innocent Chrysos Heirs hidden among the Skyfolk.
:'''Solabis:''' These schemes only came to light long after the damage was done.
:'''Phainon:''' Before the Flame-Chase Journey began, the Chrysos Heirs waged war against each other over who was a "legitimate" heir of the prophecy. Even Tribbie's many selves were pulled into the chaos.
:'''Phainon:''' At the time, golden blood was seen as a curse. Honestly? It's easy to see why.
:'''Hyacine:''' But Seliose... where was she in all of this? What thoughts weighed on her mind as she watched everything unfold?
:'''Lunabis:''' You'll know very soon, Miss Hyacine.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Witness the true history of the Skyfolk.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Listen to Hyacine's summary.
:{{tx}}

:'''Solabis:''' Her unconditional tolerance was met with ruthless betrayal.
