::'''Hyacine:''' ..."The turn of dawn and dusk, commanding the celestial globe..."
::'''Hyacine:''' "Reveal the history, Celestial Mural."
::'''Phainon:''' Now, you have nowhere to hide... Titan.
::'''Mem:''' Look, everyone, over there &mdash;
::'''Hyacine:''' Are those... Lady Lunabis and Lord Solabis?
::'''Phainon:''' Yes, those are remnants of their memories from a thousand years ago.
::'''Indignant New Believer:''' Your Highness, what are you planning to do!?
::'''Indignant New Believer:''' We are devout disciples of Lady Seliose... We would never betray her! It's those rats... they are the fools who backstabbed our hero!
::'''Desperate Old Believer:''' Please spare us! We were blinded by hatred and misled by those people clothed in black.
::'''Indignant New Believer:''' Punish them, Your Highness! Without these stubborn remnants of the past, the Skyfolk may finally stand united under the warrior goddess's banner!
::'''Memory Solabis:''' The strong crush the weak, twisting faith into a tool for oppression.
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' The weak rise to power, yet the cycle of hatred endures, unbroken through time.
::'''Memory Solabis:''' Seliose has made her judgment &mdash;
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' &mdash; The corruption within humanity is a sickness beyond cure.
::'''Desperate Old Believer:''' Yet she once loved us with such fierce devotion...
::'''Desperate Old Believer:''' Has she... given up on us?
::'''Memory Solabis:''' Seliose touched the Coreflame and gained the vision of the Titan.
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' She saw what the god fears &mdash; rooted in the darkness, spawning from the edge of the world, the black tide that devours all.
::'''Memory Solabis:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|They flee from the clouds not out of favoritism toward the scorching sun, but merely out of fear of that boundless shadow.}}
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' Yet humanity misinterpreted the god's intentions, forging them into weapons for fratricide...
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' ...This history, brewed from sorrow and tragedy, shall end here.
::'''Indignant New Believer:''' In the name of the warrior goddess...
::'''Indignant New Believer:''' What kind of fate has she woven for us...?
::'''Memory Solabis:''' We are here to deliver the message Seliose left for mortals &mdash;
::'''Memory Solabis:''' "To my once beloved, yet now unsavable kin &mdash;"
::'''Memory Solabis:''' "With golden divine blood coursing through me, even the Tyrant of the Sky bends to my unyielding light. My light burns far brighter than before, and the fog clouding my mind has finally lifted &mdash;"
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' "I gaze upon this fragile earth through the god's hundred eyes, and resolution fills me. A hero's instinct drives me forward, compelling me to deliver your final judgment &mdash;"
::'''Memory Solabis:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"Your future flows between the boiling streams of the golden pool at your feet &mdash;"}}
::'''Memory Lunabis:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"Rejoice, for as everyone's flesh and blood merge with liquid gold &mdash;"}}
::'''Solabis & Lunabis:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|"You will finally understand what true unity means."}}
::'''Composed Old Believer:''' Ha... I've long seen this day coming.
::'''Composed Old Believer:''' This isn't your fault, Seliose. Your only mistake...
::'''Composed Old Believer:''' ...was placing far too much hope in humanity.
::'''Hyacine:''' ...
::'''Hyacine:''' Lunabis, Solabis, you...
::'''Solabis:''' Yes, we acted as Seliose's executioners.
::'''Lunabis:''' That day, countless Skyfolk fell from the dome of the Eye of Twilight, swallowed by golden lava.
::'''Lunabis:''' They spent their entire lives praying to the sky, yet their devotion never earned them wings to escape their fate.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Seliose... was like a completely different person.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Honestly, I understand her.
::'''Phainon:''' After learning about everything she went through...
::'''Phainon:''' I feel the same way as you, (Trailblazer).
::'''Hyacine:''' If this is the true history &mdash; was Seliose's fusion with Aquila truly meant to save humanity from ruin?
